Situation:
Multiple depots across the theater are supporting dispersed combat elements operating forward on contested ground lines of communication. Supply Depot Bravo and Depot Delta hold mixed stocks of ammunition and fuel; smaller forward nodes stage limited reserves. Maneuver units including Alpha Armored Brigade, Charlie Infantry Battalion, and Echo Cavalry Squadron are sustaining high operational tempo. Key routes traverse a river valley and a mountain ridge; both are vulnerable to interdiction, IED activity, and observation. Weather and terrain reduce convoy speeds on certain axes. Air resupply is limited and reserved for emergency lift. Security escorts, route clearance, and overwatch are required to open any ground route for the day.

Mission:
Deliver required ammunition and fuel from theater depots to supported units across the operational period, meeting demands while minimizing total cost. Total cost includes transport costs by route, penalties for any authorized shortages, per-vehicle deployment costs, and fixed security risk costs incurred for each activated route.

Execution/Concept:
- Depot draw constraints: Each depot cannot issue more than available stocks per supply type each day. Flows will be allocated from depots with on-hand inventory, balancing proximity and transport costs against risk and route availability.
- Demand fulfillment with controlled risk: Each unit’s daily demand for each supply type must be met. Where operational risk or capacity constraints prevent full delivery, a controlled shortfall may be accepted and will incur a penalty cost; this will be used only to preserve force protection or when cost-effective relative to risk and distance.
- Vehicle capacity and supply volumes: Bulkier or heavier supplies consume more vehicle capacity. Vehicle allocations per route-day must be sufficient to move planned volumes without exceeding per-vehicle capacity.
- Route activation and risk cost: Activating a route for the day (sending any vehicles on that route) triggers a fixed Risk Cost that covers escorts, route clearance, and overwatch. This fixed cost is incurred once per activated route per day regardless of the number of vehicles employed on that route. To reduce overhead, movements will be consolidated onto a minimal set of active routes where tactically acceptable.
- Fleet management: Vehicles are pooled theater-wide and assigned to specific depot-to-unit routes by day. Total vehicles employed each day cannot exceed the available fleet. Vehicles may only be assigned to routes that are activated for that day.
- Cost minimization approach: The plan will prioritize secure and efficient corridors, consolidating flows to amortize activation risk costs while avoiding excessive transport costs. High-priority units receive first allocation of capacity. When a route must be activated, it will be loaded to near capacity where feasible. Shortfalls will be accepted only when the combined risk and transport costs exceed the penalty for that specific demand.
- Adjustments and contingencies: Daily updates will account for depot stock changes, route status, and enemy activity. Alternate routes may be activated if primary corridors are compromised, with the associated fixed risk costs weighed against mission urgency.

